  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1254 PM MDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nCurrent upper level analysis shows broad ridging over the central\nand western US with deepening trof off the west coast. The CWA \nsits under upper level southwest flow and clear skies. Sfc \nstations report light southerly winds across much of western SD \nwith temperatures in the 60s to low 70s. \n\nWeak front will cross the CWA overnight with the only impacts \nbeing a slight drop in tomorrow's highs and a brief period of \nbreezy northwest winds overnight. Upper ridge builds over the \nregion Wednesday into Thursday with southerly return flow \nsupporting warming temps over the area.\n\nSoutherly winds pick up early Friday morning as upper level trof \napproaches with attendant sfc low and trailing cold front crossing\nthe Northern Plains. WAA ahead of the front Friday afternoon will\nsupport highs in the upper 70s to low 80s over the western SD \nplains. As the front crosses the area later Friday evening, winds \nwill shift to the northwest but remain breezy through the night, \nespecially over northwestern SD. Much cooler conditions expected \nover the weekend with low chances for light precip.",
